# Animation

Default motion stack:

- **CSS** transitions/keyframes for UI chrome (nav, title, hovers)
- **Astro view transitions** (`ClientRouter`): shared-element morphs (`transition:name` on work cover + title from Works, and home Light House media). No whole-document fade. `main` uses a short fade. Nav stays via `site-header`.
- Prefer no animation framework for general site chrome

## Future: site preload

If the site needs a loading / splash / preload state, use the **footer berry mark animation** (`BerryMark` with `animated` — per-lobe opacity fade over the cloudberry silhouette in `src/components/BerryMark.astro` / `src/lib/berry.ts`). Do not invent a separate spinner or generic loader; that berry pulse is the brand preload.

## Future: narrative project views

When building richer, scroll- or timeline-driven **individual project** experiences (storytelling layouts, sequenced reveals, scroll-linked narrative), prefer **GSAP** (GreenSock) over Framer Motion or other React-centric libraries.

- Do not add GSAP until a concrete narrative interaction needs it
- Scope GSAP to those project views; keep site-wide chrome on CSS + Astro transitions
- Prefer GSAP over Framer Motion — this site is Astro, not a React SPA
